From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Georgia Garcia <georgia.garcia@canonical.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Apr 2025 10:53:15 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] UBUNTU: SAUCE: apparmor5.1.0 [16/25]: apparmor: mqueue: call
 security_inode_init_security on inode creation

BugLink: http://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2028253

POSIX message queues currently don't call the security init hook on
the inode creation, preventing proper mediation.

Signed-off-by: Georgia Garcia <georgia.garcia@canonical.com>
Signed-off-by: John Johansen <john.johansen@canonical.com>
Signed-off-by: Paolo Pisati <paolo.pisati@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00234
Ledger-Origin: ubuntu@6d4e1d6ef17c2fb482d4ecda4e7c3e0aa172d9e5
---
 ipc/mqueue.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ipc/mqueue.c b/ipc/mqueue.c
index d1a1965c9811..ddc8667d4e91 100644
--- a/ipc/mqueue.c
+++ b/ipc/mqueue.c
@@ -600,6 +600,15 @@ static int mqueue_create_attr(struct dentry *dentry, umode_t mode, void *arg)
 		ipc_ns->mq_queues_count--;
 		goto out_unlock;
 	}
+	error = security_inode_init_security(inode, dir,
+					     &dentry->d_name, NULL,
+					     NULL);
+	if (error) {
+		iput(inode);
+		spin_lock(&mq_lock);
+		ipc_ns->mq_queues_count--;
+		goto out_unlock;
+	}
 
 	put_ipc_ns(ipc_ns);
 	dir->i_size += DIRENT_SIZE;
